{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0159yYqpEddjEiX1bqU7qWWh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task and plan my approach before writing code.\n\n**Task**: Create unit tests for `pkg/sys` - specifically `terminal_test.go` and `fileinfo_test.go`.\n\n**Required Reading**: I need to read the PRD for sys to understand the requirements. The source code for the existing files is already provided above. Let me read the PRD first.\n\n**What exists already**:\n- `pkg/sys/terminal.go` - `TerminalSize()` function using ioctl\n- `pkg/sys/fileinfo.go` - `FileInfo` struct and `Lstat()` function\n\n\n- Platform-specific implementations for Darwin and Linux with `fillFromStat` functions\n\n**Patterns from existing tests**:\n- Copyright header on lines 1-2\n- Package-level comment listing implemented PRDs\n- Table-driven tests with `t.Run`\n- White-box testing (same package, not `_test` suffix)\n- `t.TempDir()` for fixtures\n\n**Requirements**:\n1. R1: Test TerminalSize error on non-TTY (pipe)\n2. R2: Test TerminalSize success with actual TTY dimensions\n3. R3: Test Lstat error on nonexistent path\n4. R4: Test Blocks and Blksize populated for regular files\n\nI should check the PRD to understand the full scope before writing the tests.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30623,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30623},"output_tokens":11,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a73a314-b34f-4c6a-b7b5-6b761335848f","uuid":"eca6d4df-6fd8-4177-810a-a06b0a4b7f48"}
